\title{The Euclidean Algorithm}
\date{2026-08-31T13:35:35Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{draft}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{The first algorithm we will consider is the famous \em{[Euclidean algorithm](00ET)} for finding the [greatest common divisor](00EW) of two integers.  We name it after Euclid, who wrote it down in his classic work on geometry and number theory, \em{The Elements}; however, it has been reinvented in multiple times, places and cultures throughout history.}

